% Rulings of U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CROSS, rulings.cbp.gov) run
% through the whole modelled tariff (tariff.le): Chapter 91 (clocks and
% watches and parts thereof) — watch straps of steel, leather, plastics,
% textile and rubber; watch cases, bezels, dials and hands; quartz,
% digital and automatic wrist watches; watches in other forms; alarm and
% wall clocks; a watch movement; smart watches.
%
% One scenario per ruling, which the scenario names ("scenario ny_n352742
% is, as stated in ruling NY N352742:"); each good is described by the
% facts the ruling states, each quoting its passage ("confer \"...\""), and
% the office's judgments — essential character, answers to claims — say who
% made them ("according to CBP"). The ruling's code is NOT a fact: it is in
% the comment "% CBP: <good> -> <code>" above each scenario; the
% expectation is the six-digit subheading the model derives, and where it
% differs from CBP's the comment says so (DISAGREES) and why.
%
% Selection (November 2026): rulings on the marketplace goods of Chapter 91
% that CROSS serves by number, found by web search (the CROSS search
% service asks for a browser token): watch straps and bracelets, watch cases
% and parts, wrist watches of each kind, clocks, a movement, smart watches.
% No ruling on a watch repair kit was found. Transcribed by hand, with
% every quotation checked against the ruling's text by the verifier.
%
% DISCLAIMER. This program is an example of Logical English. It is provided
% "as is", without warranty of any kind, express or implied, including any
% warranty that it is accurate, complete, up to date or fit for a particular
% purpose. It is not an official reading of the tariff or of the rulings it
% cites, it is not a binding classification ruling, and it is not legal or
% customs advice. Its answers may be wrong: do not rely on them for a real
% import, export or declaration; consult the official texts, the customs
% authority and a qualified professional. Its authors accept no liability for
% any loss or damage arising from its use.

the target language is: prolog.
scenario facts require provenance.

the knowledge base cbp 91 includes these resources:
    tariff.

the knowledge base cbp 91 includes:

